<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91229" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτολί-πορθος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέρθω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sacking</i> or <i>wasting cities</i>, epith. of
			Ares, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				20.152
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				936
			</span></i>; of Odysseus and Oïleus, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.278
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				728
			</span></i>; of Achilles, <i><span class="en">
				15.77
			</span></i>, etc.; also of Heracles, <u>Tab.Defix.</u> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stud.Ital.</u>
				2(1922).394
			</span></i> (Cret., <span class="entity">iv/iii B.C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. μάχαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					8.35
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτολίπορθον στίχα Μήδων</span>
			Epigr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				11.14
			</span></i>:— also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτολι-πόρθης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				472
			</span></i> (lyr.); as pr.n. of a son of Odysseus, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				8.12.6
			</span></i>:—the form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολίπορθος</span> never occurs, for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτολίπορθ᾽</span> (voc.) is rightly restored in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				783
			</span></i> (lyr.); cf. sq.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
